man territories through his support of the First Mithridatic War against Pontus. Despite being defeated at the Battle of Magnesia in 190 BCE, Strabo continued to shape Roman politics until his death in 200 BCE. He is remembered for his efforts to reform the Roman constitution and promote a more democratic system.

